--- compress -- compression contract.
---
--- Format-agnostic codec signatures plus the laws every backend must
--- satisfy. Backends (`compress-zlib-c`, `compress-gzip-c`, a future
--- pure-handl `compress-gzip`, ...) export `compress`/`decompress` arrows
--- of these types; a backend conforms to the contract by instantiating
--- the laws.
---
--- `~[1]~>` marks the codec arrows as effectful: every current backend
--- reaches a foreign library through `ffi.call`.

export Compress   := (Bytes) ~[1]~> Bytes
export Decompress := (Bytes) ~[1]~> Bytes

--- The identity arrow, named so the laws can mention it.
export id := (x) ~> x

--- decompress is a left inverse of compress: decoding what a conforming
--- encoder produced returns the input bytes. Quantified over the contract
--- signatures so any backend can be checked against it.
export roundtrip := (compress: Compress, decompress: Decompress) ~>
  (compress >>> decompress) ~[2]~> id

--- Derived form: compress absorbs a trailing decompress ∘ compress
--- round-trip. Follows from `roundtrip` by right-composition with
--- compress.
export absorb := (compress: Compress, decompress: Decompress) ~>
  (compress >>> decompress >>> compress) ~[2]~> compress
